Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course!  Here’s an example of an if/then statement in C:

```
int x = 5;
if (x < 0) {
  printf("x is negative");
} else {
  printf("x is positive");
}
```

You can replace the value of x with any integer value you’d like.  Here’s another example:

```
int y = 0;
if (y == 0) {
  printf("y is zero");
} else {
  printf("y is not zero");
}
```

That version uses an if/else statement to check if y is equal to zero, if it is, it prints “y is zero” and if it isn’t, it prints “y is not zero”.
